# The published page is compared byte for byte — by the CI drift guard and by the test beside
# it. The build writes LF explicitly so the rebuild matches on any OS; without this line a
# Windows checkout converts the committed copy to CRLF, and every local rebuild then reports a
# stale page for a reason no commit caused.
docs/index.html text eol=lf

# The metrics are the page's only input, and the analysis writes them with LF for the same
# reason: a file that changes line endings on checkout is a file the page silently disagrees
# with.
reports/metrics/*.json text eol=lf
